## Step 2: Write the hook

The premise is live within the first fifteen seconds — about **40 words** at 170 wpm. Not the topic, the *premise*. The topic is "fear." The premise is "your brain is still running Stone Age settings, and here is the proof."

Never open with:

> Today we're going to talk about... / Have you ever wondered... / In this video, we'll explore... / Picture this. / Throughout history, humans have always...

### Channel cold open (Mode C)

| Time | Job | Example (Video #1) |
|---|---|---|
| 0–5 s | The viewer's own moment of the thing, concrete and recent | "Last night, a sound in the dark made your heart jump. There was nothing there." |
| 5–15 s | The shadow reveal — the ancestor behind the reaction — and the premise | "Your brain wasn't broken. It was doing exactly what it was built for, in a world your ancestors lived in for hundreds of thousands of years." |
| 15–30 s | A rapid three-item preview and the promise the video will pay | "Every fear on this list once kept someone alive. By the end, you'll know which ones you inherited — and which one is quietly running your life." |
| by ~1:45–2:00 | First hard evidence payoff: a named study, a number, a twist | The lion-attack study in the dark segment |

The first evidence payoff is not optional. Up to that point the viewer is running on the promise; the study is where they decide you're worth trusting for ten minutes.

### Other hook shapes (Modes A and B, or for variety)

**The demolished assumption.** Name what the viewer believes, then knock it over.
> Lighthouse keeping sounds like the perfect job for people who hate people. It was — in the same way solitary confinement is technically alone time.

**The impossible fact, stated flatly.**
> In 1518 a woman walked into a street in Strasbourg and started dancing. Within weeks, dozens of people had joined her.

**The immediate predicament.** Mode B's default.
> You hatch in total darkness two thousand feet down, already starving, and the only useful skill you were born with is the ability to smell a female and bite her.

**The contradiction.**
> The most glamorous, best-paying job available to a young woman in 1922 mostly involved painting tiny numbers on watch faces. It also dissolved her jaw.

**The absurd hypothetical.**
> Imagine losing a war to an enemy with no weapons, no strategy, no leadership, and no particular interest in fighting you.

Whatever shape you pick, the second beat is already moving. Don't hook and then explain the hook.

